.TH "rbc::LEGEND" 3tcl 0\&.8\&.5 "rbc" "Upgraded Tcl/Tk9\&.0-ready RBC package"
.SH NAME
rbc::LEGEND - Commands in namespace rbc::LEGEND
.SH "GRAPH LEGEND LEGEND COMMAND"
.PP
Commands in this namespace document the graph legend\&.
.PP
LEGEND is used below as a placeholder for:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
GRAPHINST legend
.fi
.RE
.PP
The legend displays an entry for graph elements\&. Each entry contains the element's symbol and label and uses the
drawing attributes of that element\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
graph \&.g
\&.g element create signal1 -x {0 1 2 3} -y {1 4 2 5} -label "Input"
\&.g element create signal2 -x {0 1 2 3} -y {3 2 5 4} -label "Output"
\&.g legend configure -position rightmargin -font {TimesNewRoman 10}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each graph has one global legend\&. A \fI::rbc::TRACKGRAPH\fP widget also has an optional local legend for each named track;
see Track-local legends below\&.
.PP
With -renderer cairo, legend line samples, geometric and bitmap symbols, and bar swatches use Cairo\&. They
follow -antialias and the normal element pen, including dash colors and stipples\&. Swatch stipples restart at
the sample origin\&. Text, backgrounds, and relief borders remain native\&. The same behavior applies to external
legend windows\&.
.SH "TRACK-LOCAL LEGENDS"
.PP
Each \fI::rbc::TRACKGRAPH\fP track (row or inverted column) owns a legend addressed through TRACKGRAPH legend
trackName\&. It accepts the same configure, cget, get, activate, deactivate, and bind operations as
the global legend:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -hide yes
\&.g track legend voltage configure -hide no -position right -anchor ne -background white
\&.g track legend current configure -hide no -position top -anchor nw -rows 1
\&.g track legend voltage bind all <ButtonPress-1> {
    puts [\&.g track legend voltage get current]
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Local legends default to -hide yes, -position plotarea, -anchor ne, and -raised yes\&. They use the
same font, color, symbol, padding, border and row/column options as the global legend\&. Their option-database
component is trackLegend, class TrackLegend\&. Configure each track legend separately for different styles\&.
.PP
A local legend contains only its track's displayed elements with nonempty labels, in element display order\&.
-hideplot yes retains an entry so an active legend can show that element again\&. Moving an element to
another track moves its entry; deleting the element or clearing its label removes the entry\&. Empty legends
occupy no space\&. Reordering or resizing tracks carries each legend along without replacing its bindings\&.
.PP
Local -position accepts plotarea, left, right, top, or bottom, all \fBinside the track\fP\&. With
plotarea, -anchor positions the legend within the entire row\&. The other positions pin it to the named
edge; -anchor chooses its position along that edge\&. Margin positions, @x,y, and external windows are
not supported for local legends\&. The global legend retains all its existing positions and external-window
behavior\&. Local legends overlay the plot and do not reserve margins or change shared X alignment\&.
.PP
Drawing and picking are clipped to the owning row, including when labels are too large to fit\&. Native and
Cairo drawing, and SVG/PDF/PostScript output, use the same membership and layout\&. -raised selects drawing
above or below elements, as for a global plot legend\&. If global and local legends overlap, the raised one
receives legend events; at equal -raised values the global legend takes precedence\&.
.PP
TRACKGRAPH legend trackName bbox returns the visible, clipped rectangle as x y width height in
graph-window pixels, or an empty list when nothing is visible\&. Unlike track bbox, the last two values are
dimensions, not opposite corners\&. get @x,y uses the same graph-window coordinates and never selects an
entry outside the row\&. get current refers only to the entry currently picked in that particular legend\&.
.PP
Local legend operations accept unambiguous abbreviations, including bb or bbo for bbox\&.
b is ambiguous between bbox and bind; use bi or bind for bindings\&. bbox accepts no
additional arguments\&. It is available only on local legends, not the global legend\&.
.PP
Local binding tables are scoped: binding all, an element name, its class, or one of its tags in one local
legend does not install that binding in another legend\&. Local activate/deactivate patterns select only
that track's elements\&. Label activation and element -labelrelief are shared element state, so a label's
appearance is consistent when the element is present in both a local and the global legend\&.
.PP
Global and local legends can coexist; neither is hidden automatically\&. Deleting an empty track destroys
its local legend and bindings\&. graphtoolbar -type trackgraph -activelegend supplies its normal state cycle
for local legends, including tracks created later, and does not start box zoom or pan over their rectangles\&.
See demos/trackgraph2\&.tcl for a working example\&.
.SH "LEGEND ENTRIES"
.PP
Legend entries correspond to graph elements\&. The element's -label option supplies the text displayed in the
legend\&.
.PP
The order of legend entries follows the element display order\&.
.PP
Legend entries may be made active independently of the corresponding graph elements:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend activate signal1
\&.g legend deactivate signal1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Activating a legend entry changes only the appearance of the entry in the legend\&. It does not activate the
corresponding data points or change how the element is drawn in the plotting area\&.
.PP
To activate both independently:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend activate signal1
\&.g element activate signal1
.fi
.RE
.SH "LEGEND POSITION"
.PP
The -position option determines where the legend is displayed\&.
.PP
.nf
┌──────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Position     │ Description                                                       │
├──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ leftmargin   │ Draws the legend in the left graph margin\&.                        │
│ rightmargin  │ Draws the legend in the right graph margin\&. This is the default\&.  │
│ topmargin    │ Draws the legend in the top graph margin\&.                         │
│ bottommargin │ Draws the legend in the bottom graph margin\&.                      │
│ plotarea     │ Draws the legend inside the plotting area\&.                        │
│ @x,y         │ Places the legend at the specified screen coordinates\&.            │
│ \&.window      │ Creates an external legend window with the specified Tk pathname\&. │
└──────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

.fi
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -position plotarea -anchor se
.fi
.RE
.PP
places the legend in the lower-right part of the plotting area\&.
.PP
An explicit screen position may also be used:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -position @100,100 -anchor se
.fi
.RE
.PP
For an @x,y position, negative coordinates are measured from the opposite edge of the graph\&. For example, a
negative X coordinate is relative to the right edge and a negative Y coordinate is relative to the bottom edge\&.
.PP
A pathname beginning with \&. selects an external legend window:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -position \&.legend
grid \&.g -row 0 -column 0 -sticky news
grid \&.legend -row 1 -column 0 -sticky news
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rbc creates the window at that pathname and draws the legend into it\&. If the external legend window is
destroyed, the legend returns to rightmargin\&.
.PP
The -anchor option controls how the legend is positioned relative to its selected site or screen coordinate\&.
.SH "LEGEND LAYOUT"
.PP
Legend entries are arranged as a table\&.
.PP
-rows and -columns can be used to request a particular table shape:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -columns 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
A value of 0 leaves that dimension automatic\&.
.PP
When the legend has a single row, each entry uses its own label width, plus space for its symbol, borders and
internal padding\&. For example, -rows 1 produces a compact horizontal legend\&. Multi-row legends retain
equal-width cells based on the widest label\&. Automatic layout in the top and bottom margins uses one row when
the combined individual entry widths fit the available width\&.
.PP
-ipadx and -ipady specify padding inside individual legend entries\&. -padx and -pady specify padding
around the outside of the complete legend\&.
.PP
Each padding value may contain either one screen distance or two:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -ipadx {2 6} -pady {4 8}
.fi
.RE
.PP
A single value applies equally to both sides\&. Two values specify the two sides independently\&.
.SH "ACTIVE ENTRIES"
.PP
LEGEND activate marks entries for drawing with the active legend style and returns the names of all entries
that are currently active\&.
.PP
The active appearance is controlled by:
.TP
\(bu
-activebackground
.TP
\(bu
-activeborderwidth
.TP
\(bu
-activeforeground
.TP
\(bu
-activerelief
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend configure -activebackground lightblue -activeforeground navy -activerelief raised
\&.g legend activate signal1
.fi
.RE
.PP
LEGEND deactivate restores the normal legend appearance\&.
.SH "LEGEND BINDINGS"
.PP
Event bindings may be associated with legend entries using LEGEND bind\&.
.PP
Element names act as binding tags for their corresponding legend entries:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend bind signal1 <Button-1> {
    puts "signal1"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
The element under the current pointer may be obtained with LEGEND get and used by a binding:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g legend bind all <Button-1> {
    set element [\&.g legend get current]
    puts $element
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
LEGEND get can also identify the entry at an explicit screen position\&.
.SH "LEGEND OPTIONS"
.PP
.nf
┌──────────────────────────┬───────────────────┬───────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Option                   │ Database name     │ Database class    │ Description                                       │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────┼───────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -activebackground color  │ activeBackground  │ ActiveBackground  │ Sets the background color used for active legend  │
│                          │                   │                   │ entries\&.                                          │
│ -activeborderwidth       │ activeBorderWidth │ ActiveBorderWidth │ Sets the width of the 3-D border around active    │
│ distance                 │                   │                   │ legend entries\&. The default is 2\&.                 │
│ -activeforeground color  │ activeForeground  │ ActiveForeground  │ Sets the foreground color used for active legend  │
│                          │                   │                   │ entries\&.                                          │
│ -activerelief relief     │ activeRelief      │ ActiveRelief      │ Sets the relief used for active legend entries\&.   │
│                          │                   │                   │ The default is flat\&.                              │
│ -anchor anchor           │ anchor            │ Anchor            │ Specifies how the legend is positioned relative   │
│                          │                   │                   │ to the location selected by -position\&. The        │
│                          │                   │                   │ default is center\&.                                │
│ -background color        │ background        │ Background        │ Sets the legend background color\&. An empty value  │
│                          │                   │                   │ makes the legend background transparent\&.          │
│ -bg color                │ —                 │ —                 │ Synonym for -background\&.                          │
│ -borderwidth distance    │ borderWidth       │ BorderWidth       │ Sets the width of the 3-D border around the       │
│                          │                   │                   │ legend\&. The default is 2\&.                         │
│ -bd distance             │ —                 │ —                 │ Synonym for -borderwidth\&.                         │
│ -columns number          │ columns           │ Columns           │ Specifies the requested number of columns used to │
│                          │                   │                   │ arrange legend entries\&. 0 selects the automatic   │
│                          │                   │                   │ layout\&.                                           │
│ -font font               │ font              │ Font              │ Sets the font used for legend labels\&.             │
│ -foreground color        │ foreground        │ Foreground        │ Sets the foreground color used for legend labels\&. │
│                          │                   │                   │ The default is black\&.                             │
│ -fg color                │ —                 │ —                 │ Synonym for -foreground\&.                          │
│ -hide boolean            │ hide              │ Hide              │ Controls whether the legend is displayed\&. The     │
│                          │                   │                   │ default is no\&.                                    │
│ -ipadx padding           │ iPadX             │ IPadX             │ Sets horizontal padding inside each legend entry\&. │
│ -ipady padding           │ iPadY             │ IPadY             │ Sets vertical padding inside each legend entry\&.   │
│ -padx padding            │ padX              │ PadX              │ Sets horizontal padding around the exterior of    │
│                          │                   │                   │ the legend\&.                                       │
│ -pady padding            │ padY              │ PadY              │ Sets vertical padding around the exterior of the  │
│                          │                   │                   │ legend\&.                                           │
│ -position position       │ position          │ Position          │ Specifies where the legend is displayed\&. The      │
│                          │                   │                   │ value may select a graph margin, plotarea, or an  │
│                          │                   │                   │ explicit @x,y window position\&. The default is     │
│                          │                   │                   │ right\&. In @x,y form, each coordinate accepts a    │
│                          │                   │                   │ Tcl integer expression\&.                           │
│ -raised boolean          │ raised            │ Raised            │ Controls whether a legend placed in the plotting  │
│                          │                   │                   │ area is drawn above graph elements\&. The default   │
│                          │                   │                   │ is no\&.                                            │
│ -relief relief           │ relief            │ Relief            │ Sets the relief used for the legend border\&. The   │
│                          │                   │                   │ default is sunken\&.                                │
│ -rows number             │ rows              │ Rows              │ Specifies the requested number of rows used to    │
│                          │                   │                   │ arrange legend entries\&. 0 selects the automatic   │
│                          │                   │                   │ layout\&.                                           │
│ -shadow shadow           │ shadow            │ Shadow            │ Specifies a shadow for legend labels\&. An empty    │
│                          │                   │                   │ value disables the shadow\&.                        │
└──────────────────────────┴───────────────────┴───────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

.fi
.PP
Legend configuration options may also be set through Tk's option database\&. The resource name is legend and
the resource class is Legend\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
option add *Graph\&.legend\&.Foreground navy
option add *Graph\&.Legend\&.Relief raised
.fi
.RE


